  "title": "Ashurbanipal",
  "summary": "Ashurbanipal became king of Assyria on the death of his father Esarhaddon, being crowned in 668 BCE, and ruled from Nineveh until about 627 BCE. His reign included campaigns against Egypt and Elam and a war with his brother, who ruled Babylon and died there in 648. He is credited with building a library at Nineveh of over 30,000 clay tablets.",
